00:37:56.990 --> 00:37:57.740
MARK MANDEL: Cool.

00:37:57.740 --> 00:38:00.260
So, the question of the
week we talked about,

00:38:00.260 --> 00:38:03.290
around encryption and data--
encryption of data at rest.

00:38:03.290 --> 00:38:06.020
The idea being, so, say
I have these keys, right?

00:38:06.020 --> 00:38:08.030
So, I have these
encryption keys that I

00:38:08.030 --> 00:38:10.700
want to use for encrypting
my data at rest.

00:38:10.700 --> 00:38:12.961
I know Google encrypts
data at rest generally,

00:38:12.961 --> 00:38:14.210
but I want to use my own keys.

00:38:14.210 --> 00:38:15.191
How can I do that?

00:38:15.191 --> 00:38:16.940
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah,
so that is actually

00:38:16.940 --> 00:38:19.490
something that happens
often is, sometimes

00:38:19.490 --> 00:38:21.720
some companies will have--

00:38:21.720 --> 00:38:24.410
they need to have
their own keys.

00:38:24.410 --> 00:38:26.960
And they need to be
able to access them.

00:38:26.960 --> 00:38:30.320
If you're using Google
Cloud Storage, by default,

00:38:30.320 --> 00:38:31.640
it will be encrypted.

00:38:31.640 --> 00:38:34.722
But you don't have the choice of
this is the key I want to use.

00:38:34.722 --> 00:38:35.430
MARK MANDEL: Yep.

00:38:35.430 --> 00:38:37.050
And that's the same
for disks as well.

00:38:37.050 --> 00:38:37.966
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:38:37.966 --> 00:38:41.060
It's actually basically for
every data stored at rest,

00:38:41.060 --> 00:38:42.020
is actually encrypted.

00:38:42.020 --> 00:38:44.220
So that is pretty cool.

00:38:44.220 --> 00:38:46.770
So now what we have is,
there's two options.

00:38:46.770 --> 00:38:49.520
Either you manage
completely your keys,

00:38:49.520 --> 00:38:52.770
and that is hard, because
you know, it's like--

00:38:52.770 --> 00:38:54.020
MARK MANDEL: Security is hard.

00:38:54.020 --> 00:38:56.630
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Your keys
are kind of an important thing

00:38:56.630 --> 00:38:57.364
to keep--

00:38:57.364 --> 00:38:59.780
I kept on losing my keys, like
my house keys all the time.

00:38:59.780 --> 00:39:04.111
But if you lose your encryption
keys, you know, drama.

00:39:04.111 --> 00:39:04.860
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:39:04.860 --> 00:39:07.151
And you can't just keep your
encryption keys in a bowl.

00:39:07.151 --> 00:39:08.330
Like, that doesn't--

00:39:08.330 --> 00:39:09.080
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
Yeah, that's what I do

00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:09.996
and I still lose them.

00:39:09.996 --> 00:39:13.250
But anyway, the cool
thing is that we actually

00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:17.690
announced recently a new service
which is Google Cloud Key

00:39:17.690 --> 00:39:18.950
Management Service.

00:39:18.950 --> 00:39:22.000
And what it allows you,
is to have your own keys

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:26.330
that then you can use for the
encryption at rest of your data

00:39:26.330 --> 00:39:27.860
on Google Cloud Platform.

00:39:27.860 --> 00:39:29.930
But also, you're the
one managing them.

00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:32.030
You can create them,
you can rotate them,

00:39:32.030 --> 00:39:34.070
you can delete them
if you need to.

00:39:34.070 --> 00:39:37.700
And something that I really
like is that, they are also--

00:39:37.700 --> 00:39:40.730
this service is linked
directly to IAM.

00:39:40.730 --> 00:39:43.640
Which makes it
really easy to manage

00:39:43.640 --> 00:39:45.710
who has access to what keys.

00:39:45.710 --> 00:39:50.660
And also, it is also
linked to audit logging.

00:39:50.660 --> 00:39:53.860
Which means that you not only
can control who access what,

00:39:53.860 --> 00:39:57.080
but you can also see
who did access what.

00:39:57.080 --> 00:39:59.630
Which is something that
internally at Google we

00:39:59.630 --> 00:40:02.210
use, and we know that many
other companies need to use.

00:40:02.210 --> 00:40:03.620
So it's very nice to have.

00:40:03.620 --> 00:40:03.900
MARK MANDEL: Cool.

00:40:03.900 --> 00:40:05.430
So, actually that's a
really interesting point.

00:40:05.430 --> 00:40:06.470
So, I might be--

00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:08.325
I definitely have
to have my own keys

00:40:08.325 --> 00:40:09.950
and I have to manage
to myself, because

00:40:09.950 --> 00:40:12.050
of some requirement or
some sort of audit thing.

00:40:12.050 --> 00:40:14.329
But maybe my requirements
are more just like, oh,

00:40:14.329 --> 00:40:16.370
you need to make sure you
rotate them this often,

00:40:16.370 --> 00:40:17.480
or something like that.

00:40:17.480 --> 00:40:19.450
In which case, I could
come to Google Cloud,

00:40:19.450 --> 00:40:21.716
use the Key Management
Service, have them manage that

00:40:21.716 --> 00:40:23.090
and make that
really easy for me.

00:40:23.090 --> 00:40:23.300
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:40:23.300 --> 00:40:26.000
Basically, we understand that
some people, some companies,

00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:29.300
have very strict requirements.

00:40:29.300 --> 00:40:32.150
And that means that they will
need to manage them themselves,

00:40:32.150 --> 00:40:32.990
and that is cool.

00:40:32.990 --> 00:40:35.510
But most of the time, the
requirements that they're

00:40:35.510 --> 00:40:37.880
going to have will
be met already

00:40:37.880 --> 00:40:41.260
by Google Cloud Key
Management Service,

00:40:41.260 --> 00:40:43.010
and it makes things just easier.

00:40:43.010 --> 00:40:44.385
MARK MANDEL:
Totally fair enough.

00:40:44.385 --> 00:40:45.290
All right, cool.

